        "date": "2026-11-10T13:54:18Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): one feature graph and pick API - welded faces, feature edges and points, visible-first (#692 step 1)\n\napp::pick::feature_graph builds per mesh the only pickable things:\nwelded faces (geometry::feature's facet_patch weld, the patches\nlist_features reports), feature edges (open boundaries, non-manifold\nfolds, creases between welded faces - never the strip seams of a\ntessellated wall or a flat face's diagonals), feature points (3+ edges,\nchain ends, turns past 30 degrees) and round-run centres. Cached per\nfacet digest like model::features_of_local.\n\napp::pick::feature_pick resolves a ray (perspective or ortho) to the\nfront-most surface hit, then snaps within a radius by point > centre >\nedge > face among the accepted kinds, each edge/point occlusion-tested\ntoward the eye unless `through` is set. Placements honoured as in\nfirst_hit_f; pick::ray_triangle is now pub(crate) and shared.\n\nUI pickers and MCP pick tools are untouched (step 2).\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/feature_pick.rs.\n\nRefs #692\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
